{"book":"PSA","chapter":117,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2],"records":[{"id":"PSA.117.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"הַֽלְל֣וּ אֶת־יְ֭הוָה כָּל־גּוֹיִ֑ם שַׁ֝בְּח֗וּהוּ כָּל־הָאֻמִּֽים׃","gloss":"Praise YHWH, all nations; extol him, all the peoples.","pieces":[[1,"Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, every nation! Sing {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} praises, all you peoples!",null]],"L":{"1":"Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, all nations; extol {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}, all the peoples!"},"R":{"1":"All you nations, praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}! People everywhere, give {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} honor!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191170010011"],"choice":"the shortest psalm","alternatives":[],"reason":"Psalm 117 has only two verses, the shortest chapter in the Bible. It calls every nation to praise the God of Israel.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o191170010011","o191170010031","o191170010041","o191170010051"],"choice":"quoted in Romans 15:11","alternatives":[],"reason":"Paul quotes this verse to show that the nations were always meant to praise God for his mercy (Romans 15:8-11).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191170010061"],"choice":"extol: praise aloud","alternatives":["laud"],"reason":"The verb (shibbach) is to praise loudly, to commend (63:4; 145:4).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"All nations, praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.117.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"כִּ֥י גָ֘בַ֤ר עָלֵ֨ינוּ׀חַסְדּ֗וֹ וֶֽאֱמֶת־יְהוָ֥ה לְעוֹלָ֗ם הַֽלְלוּ־יָֽהּ׃","gloss":"For mighty over us [is] his loyal love, and [the] faithfulness of YHWH [is] forever. Praise Yah!","pieces":[[2,"For {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love toward us is overwhelming, and {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} stays faithful forever. Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yah}}!",null]],"L":{"2":"For mighty over us [is] {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love, and the faithfulness of {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} [is] forever. Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yah}}!"},"R":{"2":"His faithful love for us is very great, and {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} will always be faithful. Praise {{divine_name:the LORD|Yah}}!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191170020021"],"choice":"mighty: strong, prevailing","alternatives":["great"],"reason":"The verb (gavar) is to be strong, to prevail. His love has proved stronger than anything against his people (103:11).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191170020041"],"choice":"loyal love: chesed","alternatives":["steadfast love","kindness","mercy"],"reason":"The word (chesed) is the love that keeps faith, God's commitment to his people that does not give up (5:8).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191170020032"],"choice":"us: Israel, among the nations","alternatives":[],"reason":"The nations are called to praise for the love shown to \"us\", God's people. Paul saw in it the joining of the nations with Israel (Romans 15:10-11).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191170020081","o191170020091"],"choice":"Praise the LORD: Hallelu-yah","alternatives":["Hallelujah"],"reason":"The Hebrew is two words: a plural command, \"praise!\" (hallelu), and Yah, the short form of the divine name (as in 68:5 and Exodus 15:2). It calls the gathered people to praise. Like the full name, Yah is rendered \"the LORD\", with Yah as the alternative.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191170020041"],"choice":"faithful love","alternatives":["loyal love"],"reason":"As in the earlier psalms, Readable says \"faithful love\" for chesed.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o191170010011","text":"הַֽלְל֣וּ","after":" ","lemma":"הָלַל","morph":"Vpv2mp","gloss":"praise","strong":"1984a","transliteration":"haləlû","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Piel · imperative · 2nd person masculine plural"},{"id":"o191170010021","text":"אֶת","after":"־","lemma":"אֵת","morph":"To","gloss":"(et)","strong":"0853","transliteration":"ʾeṯ-","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · direct object marker"},{"id":"o191170010031","text":"יְ֭הוָה","after":" ","lemma":"יהוה","morph":"Np","gloss":"Yahweh","strong":"3068","transliteration":"yhwh","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o191170010041","text":"כָּל","after":"־","lemma":"כֹּל","morph":"Ncmsc","gloss":"O.all","strong":"3605","transliteration":"kol-","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o191170010051","text":"גּוֹיִ֑ם","after":" ","lemma":"גּוֹי","morph":"Ncmpa","gloss":"nations","strong":"1471","transliteration":"gôyim","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine plural absolute"},{"id":"o191170010061","text":"שַׁ֝בְּח֗וּ","after":"","lemma":"שָׁבַח","morph":"Vpv2mp","gloss":"extol","strong":"7623","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Piel · imperative · 2nd person masculine plural"},{"id":"o191170010062","text":"הוּ","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp3ms","gloss":"him","strong":"1930a","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 3rd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o191170010071","text":"כָּל","after":"־","lemma":"כֹּל","morph":"Ncmsc","gloss":"O.all","strong":"3605","transliteration":"kol-","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o191170010081","text":"הָ","after":"","lemma":"הַ","morph":"Td","gloss":"the","strong":"1886a","transliteration":"hā","lang":"H","parse":"Particle ·